'''True Assassin''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Fate/Stay Night: Heaven's Feel Collaboration Event/Gacha Drop|Fate/Stay Night: Heaven's Feel]] collaboration gacha event. He was added in [[Version 15.4 Update|Version 15.4]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 865
|rarity = UR
|name1 = True Assassin
|name2 = True Assassin CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''True Assassin CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
While his stats are not very good, True Assassin makes up for it through an impressive array of crowd-control abilities tailored to Floating and Alien. He maintains a 38%/96% uptime on [[Freeze]]/[[Weaken]] with a 100% activation rate, which, for a superbackliner, is quite decent all around. He's capable of sniping backline Aliens like [[I.M. Phace]] and [[Project A]] with his high-pierce attacks, but does tend to struggle against the melees that infest much of the Floating trait given his massive blind spot. Even with the [[Dodge Attack]] ability, he has a terrible base HP and lacks immunities outside of [[Immune to Toxic|Toxic Immune]]. A 60% Dodge chance is also not good enough to warrant using him in stages with enemies that can clip him, since depending on the matchup, it's entirely likely they one-tap him out of existence.

True Assassin still isn't bad per se, but he requires you to protect him extensively and is prone to spontaneously dying unless boosted. He won't be playing much of an attacking role in any lineup either, given his low DPS.

{{Job|Classification = Sniper & Crowd-Controller}}

